// Rule 1: PHP file created in the web root by any account (auditd)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Finding:        Both web shells were written by root: health-check.php at
//                 04:34:31 (through an SSH session with sudo) and the shell
//                 re-created in visit 3. The cookie backdoor was written into
//                 wp-includes/version.php at 04:37:19.
// Data source:    auditd PATH records (HartwellAudit_CL), Microsoft Sentinel.
// Time column:    OriginalTime (TimeGenerated is ingestion time in this data).
// Hunt window:    2026-10-23 04:00 to 16:00 UTC.
// Result:         6 rows. Caught both web shell writes and the version.php
//                 backdoor. Three root-created files about 24 minutes before
//                 the scan are unexplained; they need checking against site
//                 maintenance before being treated as false positives.
// What it missed: It missed nothing it was built to catch.
// Why any account: both shells were written by root, so a rule limited to the
//                 web server account would have missed them.
// Expected false positives: WordPress core, plugin and theme updates. Exclude
//                 them by the deployment account or path once known.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
HartwellAudit_CL
| where OriginalTime between (datetime(2026-10-23T04:00:00Z) .. datetime(2026-10-23T16:00:00Z))
| where AuditType == "PATH"
| where RawLine contains "name=\"/var/www/html/" and RawLine contains ".php\"" and RawLine contains "nametype=CREATE"
| project OriginalTime, AuditSerial, RawLine
| order by OriginalTime asc
